To capture how long the user spent on the page before clicking, we can use **client-side JavaScript** to track the start time when the page loads and calculate the duration when the user clicks an element. Since **Google Apps Script (GAS)** runs on the server, we need to **send the data to a GAS web app** (via an HTTP POST request) and then process it on the server. This approach ensures data security and proper handling of server-side operations.

---

### ✅ **Step-by-Step Plan**

1. **Track Start Time**  
   Use `window.onload` to capture the time the user first loads the page.

2. **Calculate Duration on Click**  
   When the user clicks the card, compute the difference between the current time and the start time.

3. **Send Data to Google Apps Script Web App**  
   Use `fetch()` (or `XMLHttpRequest`) to send the duration and other data to a GAS web app.

4. **Process Data in GAS**  
   The web app writes the data to the appropriate Google Sheets.

---

### 🔧 **Client-Side HTML + JavaScript (Frontend)**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Page with Click Tracking</title>
    <script>
      // Store the start time when the page loads
      let startTime = null;

      window.onload = function () {
        startTime = new Date(); // Record start time
      };

      document.querySelector('.col.contentCard').addEventListener('click', function () {
        const userEmail = 'user@example.com'; // Replace with actual user email
        const currentTime = new Date();
        const duration = (currentTime - startTime) / 1000; // Duration in seconds

        const title = this.querySelector('.card-title').textContent;
        const tags = this.querySelector('.badge').textContent;
        const searchBarContents = document.querySelector('#search-bar').value;
        const category = this.dataset.category;

        // Send data to Google Apps Script web app
        fetch('https://script.google.com/macros/s/your-web-app-url/exec', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: {
            'Content-Type': 'application/json',
          },
          body: JSON.stringify({
            userEmail,
            currentTime,
            duration,
            title,
            tags,
            searchBarContents,
            category,
          }),
        }).catch((error) => {
          console.error('Error sending data:', error);
        });
      });
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <!-- Your existing HTML structure -->
    <input type="text" id="search-bar" />
    <div class="col contentCard" data-category="Other">
      <div class="card h-100 rounded-0">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h5 class="card-title">Test</h5>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
```

---

### 📌 **Server-Side Google Apps Script (GAS Web App)**

1. **Create a new Google Apps Script project** and paste the following code:

```javascript
function doPost(e) {
  const data = JSON.parse(e.postData.contents);

  // Sheet 1: All data (including duration)
  const sheet1 = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet().getSheetByName('AllData');
  sheet1.appendRow([
    data.userEmail,
    data.currentTime,
    data.duration,
    data.title,
    data.tags,
    data.searchBarContents,
    data.category
  ]);

  // Sheet 2: Individual categories (split by category)
  const sheet2 = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet().getSheetByName('Categories');
  const categories = data.category.split(',').map(c => c.trim());
  categories.forEach(category => {
    sheet2.appendRow([
      data.userEmail,
      data.currentTime,
      data.title,
      data.tags,
      data.searchBarContents,
      category
    ]);
  });

  return ContentService.createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ status: 'success' }));
}
```

2. **Deploy as a Web App**:
   - Go to **Publish > Deploy as web app**.
   - Set **Execute as** to `Me (the owner)`.
   - Set **Who has access** to `Anyone` or `Anyone who has the link`.
   - Save the deployment URL (e.g., `https://script.google.com/macros/s/your-web-app-url/exec`).

3. **Replace** the `your-web-app-url` in the client-side script with the actual URL from your GAS deployment.

---

### 📝 Notes

- **Duration Calculation**: The duration is stored in seconds (`(currentTime - startTime) / 1000`).
- **Data Security**: This approach ensures that all sensitive operations (like writing to Sheets) happen on the server.
- **User Email**: Replace the placeholder `user@example.com` with a real user email (e.g., from an authentication system or session).

---

### ✅ Final Result

- **Sheet 1 (AllData)**: Contains all data including the time spent on the page.
- **Sheet 2 (Categories)**: Each row corresponds to a single category, even if the card has multiple tags.

